 "notes": "Single sheet; decimal-inch values (no unit statement printed, so title.units not set). Numbers recorded as printed (.438 -> 0.438). Title: only the sheet-edge identifier, 'Rev C' and 'NIST PMI Test Models - 2012'; 'Test Model 3' / 'PMI Complex Test Case 3' are captions (title block not complete). The black text 'Datum Feature F not referenced - justifies placing MCS at center of large hole on flange' is test commentary, not recorded (notes not complete). Frames: 2X Ø.438 ±.005 position Ø.05(M) A B(M) C(M) (datum-reference modifiers on B and C not encoded); 4X Ø.625 ±.005 position Ø.05(M) D B C with text 'SWITCH MOUNTING LOCATIONS'; flatness '.005 / .25 X .25' is a per-unit-area flatness (tolerance .005 over a .25 x .25 area; recorded tolerance 0.005 only); profile .01 is on datum A, '2 COPLANAR SURFACES'; profile .03 A B C is on datum D; profile .06 A B C on datum E; perpendicularity Ø.01 E on datum F (Ø1.065 ±.003); position .03 D B C (no Ø) is attached to an unvalued width dimension across the Ø1.500 hole. '4X .82 ±.06' has a small circle-with-line symbol on its extension line (looks like a dimension-origin / between mark) - recorded as a plain linear ± dimension with count 4. '(.750)' is a reference dimension. tolerance.tightest = Ø1.065 ±.003 (band .006). Naming rule used for Ø callouts: a callout with an 'nX' count, THRU / depth, or an uppercase (hole) fit is recorded as hole.diameter {diameter, count, upper, lower}; any other Ø size is a dimension {type:'diameter'}. Tolerances are recorded as signed deviations upper/lower; limit dimensions as max/min. GD&T: characteristic in words, datums = the datum letters in order (datum-reference modifiers not encoded), modifiers 'MMC' / 'LMC' = circled M / L after the tolerance value, diameterZone true only where Ø precedes the tolerance."
